        "source_id": "npr_short_wave",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.npr.org/2026/11/24/nx-s1-6042518/thanksgiving-american-wild-turkey-science",
        "published_at": "2026-11-24T08:00:00",
        "level": "B2",
        "slot_level": "B2",
        "source_level": "B2",
        "word_count": 82,
        "duration_sec": 901,
        "body_text": null,
        "audio_url": "https://npr.simplecastaudio.com/72da6803-9aa4-4e2e-a973-3bc436f0e9fa/episodes/61f84333-b405-483b-a331-15d1c2df8c7d/audio/128/default.mp3/default.mp3_ywr3ahjkcgo_cF9mX3NraXA9aSAg_5375e364a2e7bb0826a4f0d74b43cf81_14420879.mp3?awCollectionId=72da6803-9aa4-4e2e-a973-3bc436f0e9fa&awEpisodeId=61f84333-b405-483b-a331-15d1c2df8c7d&feed=F0qJcgXZ&t=podcast&e=nx-s1-6042518&p=510351&d=901&size=14420472&hash_redirect=1&x-total-bytes=14420879&x-ais-classified=unclassified&x-access-range=0-1023&listeningSessionID=0CD_382_327__3bcfa83830351c67002b8bca22ed9ff1779a88ec",
        "description": "As a teen, Mike Chamberlain spent all his free time hunting turkeys. Now, his job is researching everything about them – the birds’ behavior, their genetics and more. And for the past decade, he’s focused on their concerning decline in the American southeast. Today on the show, Emily chats with Mike about what could be driving the loss of turkey territory – and what conservationists – including hunters – are doing about it. Interested in more conservation science? Email us your question at shortwave@npr.org .",
